<title>JAPAN: Nippon Oil shares rise on Burma gas output plan.</title>
<headline>Nippon Oil shares rise on Burma gas output plan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nippon Oil Co Ltd rose in Wednesday morning, supported by its plans to start commercial production of natural gas off Burma in 1999, together with Texaco Inc of the United States and Britain's Premier Oil Plc.</p>
<p>The share price was up six yen at 667 at 0042 GMT, on a volume of 488,000 shares.</p>
</text>
